.TH FMT_OCTAL 3
.SH NAME
fmt_octal \- format an unsigned 64-bit integer as an octal string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <fmt.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t fmt_octal(char* " dest ", uint64 " i ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fmt_octal
formats the unsigned 64-bit integer
.I i
as an octal (base-8) ASCII string and writes it to the buffer pointed to by
.IR dest .
.PP
If
.I dest
is not NULL, the octal representation is stored there. The function does not append a null terminator to the resulting string.
.PP
The number of bytes required for the conversion is calculated automatically before writing to the buffer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes written to the buffer (the length of the octal representation).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fmt_ulong (3),
.BR fmt_xlong (3)